# Round glmpp3: GLM-5.3-Flash's prompt groups of two by default (BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP unset runs the registry's
# 2, as V4.1 does), the plan reserving the two units a group of two holds past the first
# (place::prompt_reserve_bytes: the GEMM front and 2 x unit_bytes = 134,365,184 B at 512 columns, 9..11 card
# experts at 15.2 MB; the gate plan's e2e slot-map line moved 926 -> 915). Against the base, glmunion's commit
# (1795d258, main at the sitting), whose GLM loads run groups of one.
# Decomposition [derived, round report section 1]. At G1 a routed layer-batch is the card front, then
# max(host union + exchange 1.1, card shadow): F_KDA 5.8, F_latent 15 + 3.54 ms a batch of depth, union 48.6 ms
# (the lane law of the 3090 diagnostic, 10.74 us a slot + 72.2 us an expert, Q6_K layers x1.43) + 3.7 ms
# unattributed, 28 ms a batch outside the leg spans; the model gives 2764 ms a batch at P = 4096 against the
# sitting's 2764 (185.23 tok/s). At G2 two units are in flight, and a layer's period is
# max(one unit's loop F + max(U, S) + 1.1, the host's 2U, the card's 2(F + S + 1)): 233 of 336 layer-batches are
# host-bound (the KDA layers: the front and exchange hide under the other unit's union), 103 card-bound (the
# latent layers at depth). The model holds glmgroup's measured G2 walk (34.15 s at P = 4096 before the GEMM front
# and lanes) to -2.9..+3.1 % over the band of how much the card's spans swell when two units share it
# (front x1.028, shadow x1.00..x1.15, union x1.016, from glmgroup's G2 rows against its G1 rows).
# pp4096 2764 -> 2427..2561 ms a batch = 200..211 tok/s (+8..+14 %). pp512 is one batch, a group of one under
# either lever: its path is the base's but for the 9..11 card experts the reserve takes (derived -0.3..0 %), and so
# is decode's (host slots +0.1 %: derived, under the ruler).
kind: ab
question: do two batches in flight hide the card front and the exchange under the other batch's host union on
  the KDA layers, and the union under the card on the latent ones, now that the union is the lane kernel's?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, prose prompt (GLM_PROSE from GLM_PROSE_FROM), A6000, plan (a), --ctx 4352, each arm's
  own default group (BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP unset: the base runs 1, this round 2) - (glmpp3 - base) / base,
  paired by round across the two invocations
unit: %
predict: +8..+14
rounds: 2
condition: one hold, two runner invocations back to back, each carrying this card: the base from a tree at
  1795d258 (/Users/hckim/repo/bloomery-pp3base, its own remote dir), then this round's from /Users/hckim/repo/bloomery-glmpp3
  (BLOOMERY_REMOTE='~/repo/bloomery-glmpp3'), each BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2
  BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352 BLOOMERY_DECODE_N=3 BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/glmpp3-pp.card'
  just depth-gpu-glm5next 512 4096, BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP unset in both. Every row's load line prints group=1
  (base) or group=2 (this round), and its time prompt record kind=batch with 1 pass at P = 512 and 8 at 4096;
  this round's plan line prints 9..11 card experts fewer than the base's (the reserve: 2603 at ctx 4352 here),
  nothing else on the plan moves. A row marked [cold], [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] is void, and so is a window whose card witness or
  cpu-freq differs between the two invocations. The pp512 and decode rows must agree with the base's within the
  window's ~5 % (one batch is a group of one under either lever). Box time ~14..20 min [derived: per invocation
  two warm-up processes and four rows, six loads at 45..75 s, 2 x (4 + 22..25) s of prompt; plus the two builds]
decide-in: land it; G2 is then the floor of the flow at 512-position units: the KDA layers bound by the host
  union, the latent ones by the card. The next prompt terms are the union's per-expert term (72 us an expert,
  a quarter of the union: the pack and the expert's bytes), the Q6_K layers' downs (x1.43), and on the latent
  layers at G2 the card's shared expert and k_b, v_b
decide-below: under +8 %: the card's two streams slow each other more than the shadow's x1.15 span swell says,
  or the KDA layers are not host-bound: run one BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 P = 4096 row at G2 on this tree and read
  wait_ms (the host idle on the card) per layer kind against card_front_ms + card_shadow_ms before landing
decide-above: past +14 %: the 3.7 ms a layer-batch the lane law leaves unattributed sat in the card front (the
  fronts then hide whole at G2), or the checkpoint waits fell as glmgroup's G2 run showed (220 against 462 ms):
  read ckpt_ms from one G2 stats row and refit; land either way
